  "scope": [
    "The counted-loop legality proof establishes that the initial index cannot recur. Only direct comparisons and identity-preserving local copies use this fact; callee profitability summaries do not authorize folds.",
    "The peeled first iteration is copied before folding. Side-effect order, checked operations, state layouts, and reference alias assumptions are preserved.",
    "This remains backend-selected MIR scheduling for native LLVM. Portable MIR and Binaryen retain their previous schedule.",
    "Four processor-bank controls have byte-identical LLVM IR. Timing variation in those controls is not evidence of changed generated code.",
    "Routing-state pruning and cached-output elimination remain future work. These measurements do not establish performance on every target or source program."
  ]
